GROUND
Logical Ground Seqment sends Power message to Command and 
    Data Handling (CDH) subsystem (i.e. host).

HOST
Host messages the Payload_X (emulator) using the Shutdown message. 

PAYLOAD
Payload_X recieves the Shutdown message. Then sends the ACK command with
    id of the Shutdown message

HOST
Host recieves ACK message with Shutdown message_ID.
Host polls until payload responds at 1 Hz, start ID_exchange time
    if (ID_exchange time >= ID_exchange timout){
        // flag or send an interrupt, using flag for simplicity
        timeout_flag = 1;
        break;
    }

PAYLOAD
Payload_X then send the ID_exchange message back to the host system, confirming
    the idl_status=confirmed
// POSSIBLE FAULT LOCATION
Payload_X just does not send back a message

HOST
Host handles the timeout and executes fault response
    if (timeout_flag){
        execute_fault_response(); // could look like remessaging, reference NACK
    }
    
PAYLOAD
Payload_X performs the Shutdown

HOST
Host starts sending space vehicle telemerty to the ground system.